# Logs
logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
*.local

# Private — test account passwords, never publish (repo is public)
TEST_ACCOUNTS.md

# Local-only project notes for Claude, not for the public repo
CLAUDE.md

# Local tooling state
.claude/

# Heavy unused media
video/
*.mp4

# Editor directories and files
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea
.DS_Store
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?

# Local analytics API artefacts
# Python bytecode, at ANY depth. The old rule only covered
# server/__pycache__/, so ml/, ml/production/ and ml/evaluation/ leaked
# 53 .pyc files into a commit.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

.meta_snapshot.json
.counter_snapshot.json
server/.counter_snapshot.json

# The tag-enrolment queue. Derived local state like the two snapshots above,
# and the only file this API writes anywhere — see server/tracking.py.
server/.tracking.db
server/.tracking.db-wal
server/.tracking.db-shm

# Phase 2 feature cache — derived data, regenerable via `--dump` (8.7 MB)
server/ml/results/*.jsonl.gz

# Phase 15 offline research artifacts (regenerable)
# NOTE THE TRAILING /* -- excluding the DIRECTORY would stop git
# descending into it, and a negation below could never re-include
# anything. Excluding its contents leaves the door open.
server/ml/results/*

# EXCEPT the cohort tag lists. These are NOT derived data: the shadow
# log stores H(salt, tag) and cannot be reversed, so these 2,856 tags
# are the only thing that can ever reconcile its 2,476 observations.
# Re-deriving them would produce a DIFFERENT cohort, not the same one.
# 66 KB of public game identifiers, no secrets.
!server/ml/results/cohorts/
# ...but the cohort directory holds one OUTPUT too. Inputs and the
# runner are preserved; the checkpoint it produced is derived, and its
# figures are written up in the README instead.
server/ml/results/cohorts/checkpoint-*.json

# Shadow-mode observation log (diagnostic, regenerable)
server/ml/results/shadow-log.jsonl*

# Local environment. The Supabase URL and publishable key are public by design,
# but a .env file is exactly where a secret ends up by accident one day.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Browser verification scripts and their screenshots. Written per-task, run,
# then deleted -- they are never a committed dependency, and playwright is
# never a committed devDependency. One slipped in once.
verify*.mjs
probe*.mjs
shot-*.png

# Cygwin/MSYS crash dumps
*.stackdump
